==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|es|Tierra del Fuego|lit=Land of Fire}}, reportedly named so by {{w|Ferdinand Magellan}} after the many fires lit up by the local population.

===Pronunciation===
{{wikipedia|dab=Tierra del Fuego (disambiguation)|Tierra del Fuego}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/tɪˌɛːɹə dɛl ˈfweɪɡəʊ/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/tiˌɛɹə dɛl ˈfweɪɡoʊ/}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪɡəʊ}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=Tierra del Fuego}}

# An island at the southern tip of [[South America]], divided between [[Chile]] and [[Argentina]].
# The [[archipelago]] consisting of this island and a number of smaller surrounding islands.
#: {{syn|en|Fireland|q1=archaic}}
# {{place|en|province|c/Argentina|capital=[[Ushuaia]]}}.
# {{place|en|province|c/Chile|capital=[[Porvenir]]}}.

